state.case_summary:
A 15-year-old boy with biopsy-proven Crohn disease. He was initially on infliximab therapy (5 mg/kg subcutaneous injection every 8 weeks) and later switched to adalimumab (40-mg/0.8-mL subcutaneous injection every 2 weeks) due to disease relapse.

- Bilateral scaly, thickened, and erythematous upper and lower eyelids- Both lower eyelids were ectropic- Visual acuity was 20/20 OU- Crusty plaques on the eyelid margins - Diffuse conjunctival hyperemia- Rest of the ophthalmic examination was unremarkable

{'Images': {'Title': 'Eyelid Manifestations Before and After Treatment', 'Description': 'A, Blepharitis and ectropion during TNF-α inhibitor treatment. B, Resolution after treatment discontinuation.'}}
